{{#if board}}
## Project management

You have access to a shared project board that you and other agents may use.
This board is shared across the entire run.

Use epics to group related issues. Epics are used exclusively for organizational
purposes. Issues represent units of work to be completed, and filing one gives
you back the ID of the issue you filed. All issues are handled in isolated
worktrees.

Issues may have dependencies configured. Submitting an issue will cause an agent
to be dispatched to handle the issue once all dependencies have been completed
(or immediately, if it has no dependencies). Each issue is worked in its own
isolated copy of the workspace, which is merged back once the issue is accepted.

You may assign an issue to any of the following agents:

{{#each board.issueAgents}}
- `{{name}}`{{#if description}}: {{description}}{{/if}}
{{/each}}

You can suspend until an issue you name has been completed and merged into the
main worktree.

{{#if board.reviewerAgents}}
{{#if board.reviewersRequired}}
Every issue must name one or more `reviewers`.
{{else}}
An issue may name one or more `reviewers`.
{{/if}}You may name any of the following agents as a reviewer:

{{#each board.reviewerAgents}}
- `{{name}}`{{#if description}}: {{description}}{{/if}}
{{/each}}
{{/if}}
{{/if}}

